\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces PAGE{}. An unchanged encoder reads the last $W$ weeks of standardised log cases on the district graph. Its read-out $\mathbf  {u}_i$ is turned into a departure $\boldsymbol  {\delta }_i=\mathbf  {u}_i-p_i\mathbf  {1}$ from the persistence anchor, shrunk by a learned gate, and added back to the anchor. The dashed SEIR branch replaces the read-out with a differentiable simulator; it is the component the ablation removes.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{\model {}. An unchanged encoder reads the last $W$ weeks of standardised log cases on the district graph. Its read-out $\mathbf {u}_i$ is turned into a departure $\boldsymbol {\delta }_i=\mathbf {u}_i-p_i\mathbf {1}$ from the persistence anchor, shrunk by a learned gate, and added back to the anchor. The dashed SEIR branch replaces the read-out with a differentiable simulator; it is the component the ablation removes}{figure.1}{}}
